RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.4882923Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.4894111Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.4999412Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5012323Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5013340Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5014302Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5014714Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5015080Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5016361Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5016871Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5017209Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5017872Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5018220Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5018960Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5019880Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5020683Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5021545Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5021883Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5022176Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5022643Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5022987Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5023639Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5023881Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5024058Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5024331Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5024868Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5025729Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5026207Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5026377Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5026585Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5026865Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5027484Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5027934Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5028332Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5028605Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5028869Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5029265Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5029662Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5041905Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5042790Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5053425Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5053994Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5054469Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5055576Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5056164Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5073711Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5084416Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5085311Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5085835Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5086419Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5086748Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5086994Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5087510Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5087933Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5088749Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T18:45:55.5089109Z 
